@startuml 03-clone-existing-project
title Scenario 3: Open an existing catalog-using project on the new machine

actor User
participant "git" as Git
participant "Claude Code\nsession" as Claude
participant "catalog.sh" as Cat
participant "GitHub\n(Eminakkoc/skills)" as Index
database "<project>/.claude\n+ .mcp.json\n(committed)" as Proj
database "<U+007E>/.claude" as Home

User -> Git : git clone <project>
Git --> Proj : .claude/skills, .claude/hooks,\n.claude/settings.json, .mcp.json,\n.claude/catalog.lock.json

User -> Claude : start claude in the project
Claude --> User : trust this folder?
User -> Claude : yes
Claude -> Proj : load project skills and hooks\n(already copied, nothing to fetch)
Claude --> User : approve project MCP servers from .mcp.json?
Claude --> User : install plugins from extraKnownMarketplaces\n+ enabledPlugins?
User -> Claude : approve

note over Claude, Home
  Copied files travel with the repo, but CLI tools that items
  require (e.g. agent-browser) may be missing on this machine.
  "catalog doctor" checks for that.
end note

== catalog doctor ==
User -> Claude : "check this project's catalog items"
Claude -> Cat : catalog doctor --dry-run
Cat -> Proj : read .claude/catalog.lock.json
Cat -> Index : fetch catalog.json @ lock's index SHA
Cat -> Cat : collect "requires" of installed items
loop each required tool
  alt bin on PATH
    Cat -> Cat : ok
  else missing
    Cat --> Claude : missing <tool>
    Claude --> User : install it?
    User -> Claude : yes
    Claude -> Cat : catalog doctor --yes
    Cat -> Home : install tool @ pinned,\nrecord in <U+007E>/.claude/catalog.lock.json
  end
end
Cat -> Proj : verify every file in the lock still exists
Cat --> Claude : report: ok / missing / locally edited
Claude --> User : project ready

== Optional: pick up newer pins ==
User -> Claude : "update this project's catalog items"
Claude -> Cat : catalog update --dry-run
Cat -> Index : index @ main
Cat --> Claude : composition-patterns a1b2c3d -> f9e8d7c
Claude --> User : apply?
User -> Claude : yes
Claude -> Cat : catalog update --yes
@enduml
